/// The QUALIFIED form of the same grant, and the one that needs no name bound
/// in scope at all: `import Aggregate;` alone, and every use spelled through
/// it. A path through a facade names the item the declaring module's path
/// names - one item, many spellings - so `Aggregate::Widget` is `Inner::Widget`
/// and `Aggregate::make_widget` is `Inner::make_widget`.
///
/// The function call is the load-bearing half. A type in scope position is
/// rooted at the module its head names and read from that module's offered
/// set; a `Module::function` call appends the member to the module the scope
/// segment records, and a segment recording the FACADE names a function the
/// facade never declared.
namespace ReexportBasic::Qualified;
import ReexportBasic::Aggregate;
function via_qualifier() -> i32 {
    const w: Aggregate::Widget = Aggregate::Widget::of(7);
    const m: Aggregate::Widget = Aggregate::make_widget(8);
    return w.unwrap() + m.unwrap();
}
